{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"auspicial-wily-warbler","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Follow-up: rotate externally anchored secrets flagged during value_wo state remediation\n\nDuring gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog execution, operator approval limited autonomous rotation to internally generated/self-regenerable secrets. The following names still require human/operator coordination because they are third-party credentials, externally trusted keys, or rotations that require updating external trust stores/consumers outside the safe autonomous boundary: /rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key, /rebar/prod/jira-api-token, /rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password, /rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token, /rebar/prod/gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key, /rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key, /rebar/prod/github-oauth-client-id, /rebar/prod/github-oauth-client-secret, /rebar/prod/g2p-github-pat, /rebar/prod/ci-gerrit-ssh-key, /rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat, /rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key, /rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key, /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot, /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex, /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude, /rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat, /auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET, /auth-solutions/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each listed secret has an owner-approved rotation plan that names the external trust update required, without recording secret values.\n- [ ] Each listed secret is rotated by an operator who can reissue/update the corresponding external credential or trust store.\n- [ ] Every affected consumer is restarted/redeployed and verified healthy after its rotation.\n- [ ] Completion comments record only secret names and verification evidence, never values.\n\n## Verification\n- For each secret name, verify the corresponding AWS SSM parameter version advanced or the owning external system reports a new credential/key in use.\n- Verify Gerrit, review-bot, opcert, MCP, bridge/Jira, GitHub Actions, SSO, and any OAuth consumers remain healthy after their respective rotations.","id":"899f-f964-327c-4c47","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator: rotate externally anchored secrets"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788771046509100001,"uuid":"304c408f-746b-46fb-bae3-2f1c02451e3b"}